                <pb facs="0889" n="785" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg785"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.011/105: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-05-12T15:00:00-05:45">May 12, 1932—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>74. My telegram No. 65, April 27, 3 p.m. The Nicaraguan Congress has recessed
                    until May 31, 1932. It seems that this recess was brought about by President
                    Moncada. The matter of constitutional reform is still pending in the
                    Congress.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
